hadiths[21]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22311","Abu Kamil Muzaffar ibn Mudrik narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to me, Qabisah ibn Hulb narrated to me, from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, and a man asked him and said: There is some food I feel scrupulous about, so he said: Let nothing fluctuate in yourself resembling Christianity."
"22312","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the food of the Christians, so he said: Let no food fluctuate in your chest in which you resemble Christianity."
"22313","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sufyan, Simak narrated to me, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turn to his right and to his left, and I saw him, he said: placing this upon his chest, and Yahya described the right over the left above the joint."
"22314","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabisah ibn al-Hulb, from his father, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing his right upon his left in prayer, and I saw him turn to his right and to his left."
"22315","Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Warkani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I asked him about the food of the Christians, so he said: Let no food fluctuate, or doubt, in your chest in which you resemble Christianity."
"22316","He said: And he would turn to his left and to his right, and place one of his hands upon the other."
"22317","Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Shubah, Simak ibn Harb informed me, he said: I heard Qabisah ibn Hulb narrating from his father that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said, and he mentioned charity, he said: Let none of you come with a ewe of his that bleats on the Day of Resurrection."
"22318","Zakariya ibn Yahya ibn Subayh narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Qabisah ibn al-Hulb, from his father, he said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the food of the Christians, so he said: Let no food doubt in your chest in which you resemble Christianity. He said: And I saw him placing one of his hands upon the other."
"22319","He said: And I saw him turn once to his right and once to his left."
"22320","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the food of the Christians, he said: Let no food fluctuate in your chest in which you resemble Christianity."
"22321","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, from Shubah, from Simak, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turn from both his sides."
"22322","Abdullah narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi and Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lead us, so he would take his left with his right, and he would turn from both his sides together, from his right and from his left."
"22323","Narrated to us... [source text truncated at haddathana]"
"22324","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lead us, so he would take his left with his right, and he would turn upon both his sides together."
"22325","Muhriz ibn Awn ibn Abi Awn narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Qabisah ibn Hulb, from his father, in marfu form, he said: Everything in which you resemble Christianity, let it not doubt in your chest."
"22326","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Muhammad the freedman of Banu Hashim, Yahya ibn Abd Rabbihi, narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I heard Qabisah ibn Hulb narrating from his father that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned charity, so he said: Let none of you come with a ewe of his that bellows. He said: He says: It cries out."
"22327","Yahya ibn Abdawayh the freedman of Banu Hashim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabisah ibn al-Hulb, narrating from his father, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would turn upon both his sides."
"22328","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Qabisah ibn al-Hulb narrating from his father that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turn from both his sides."
"22329","Sulayman ibn Dawud, and he is Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi, narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I heard Qabisah ibn Hulb narrating from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned charity, so he said: Let none of you come with a ewe of his that bleats."
"22330","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabisah ibn Hulb al-Tai, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turn once to his right and once to his left."
"22331","Husayn al-Jufi narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabisah ibn Hulb al-Tai, from his father, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, he would turn to his right and to his left."
